General_SiSo_Auto_Idle_TDS_with_Counters_Check
    [Documentation]
    ...  This test collects energy counters (M40003C2 M40002C1 M40003C4), while in TDS and WITHOUT launching
    ...  a Test Model and checks whether they have changed.
    ...  This test is essentially a General_Siso_Auto_NR_DL_Test_Model_Activation_with_Counters_Check test case
    ...  without launching and stopping a Test Model.
    ...  Version for TDD and FDD radios.
    ...  WARNING: for this testcase to succeed, the energy consumption counters listed above have to be collected.
    ...  Collection of energy consumption counters such as these can be turned off and on
    ...  by setting proper parameters in the SCF. Visit appropriate MIND page to learn more.
    ...
    ...  :param int timeout: (Optional) : timeout (in seconds) for test model startup and termination, default 30.
    ...  :param int lower_limit: (Optional) : lower value of difference range between counters, default 0.
    ...  :param int upper_limit: (Optional) : upper value of difference range between counters, default 300000.

    [Arguments]                                             ${timeout}=30
    ...                                                     ${lower_limit}=0
    ...                                                     ${upper_limit}=300000

    [Timeout]                                               24 hours

    Create admin session with default alias
    ${connection}                                           connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    Create Selenium Session                                 admin_connection=${connection}
    ...                                                     download_dir=${logs_path}


    ${counter_ids}=                                         Create List    M40003C2    M40002C1    M40003C4

    ${initial_counters}                                     Wait For Counters And Save Values to Dict
    ...                                                     counter_ids=${counter_ids}
    ...                                                     time=15min

    ${latter_counters}                                      Wait For Counters And Save Values to Dict
    ...                                                     counter_ids=${counter_ids}
    ...                                                     time=15min

    Verify Difference Between Counters
    ...                                                     counters_1=${latter_counters}
    ...                                                     counters_2=${initial_counters}
    ...                                                     lower_limit=${lower_limit}
    ...                                                     upper_limit=${upper_limit}
